# Feature 13: Update Makefile with release targets and ldflags documentation

## Summary
Updated the Makefile with release infrastructure and comprehensive ldflags documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Added LDFLAGS Documentation
- Added a detailed documentation header explaining how ldflags inject version info
- Documented the three version variables:
  - `github.com/jbctechsolutions/skillrunner/internal/presentation/cli/commands.Version`
  - `github.com/jbctechsolutions/skillrunner/internal/presentation/cli/commands.GitCommit`
  - `github.com/jbctechsolutions/skillrunner/internal/presentation/cli/commands.BuildDate`
- Included example manual build command with ldflags

### 2. Added Build Variables
- `VERSION` - defaults to `git describe --tags --always --dirty`
- `GIT_COMMIT` - defaults to `git rev-parse --short HEAD`
- `BUILD_DATE` - defaults to current UTC timestamp
- `LDFLAGS_PKG` - the package path for version variables
- `LDFLAGS` - the complete ldflags string

### 3. Added New Targets
- `build-release` - builds binary with ldflags version injection
- `release` - runs goreleaser (with GITHUB_TOKEN check)
- `release-snapshot` - runs goreleaser in snapshot mode (for testing)

### 4. Updated Help Target
- Reorganized help into categories (Development, Release, Other)
- Added documentation for build variables override

## Testing
- `make help` - works correctly, shows all new targets
- `make -n build-release` - dry run shows correct ldflags expansion
- `make -n release` - correctly checks for GITHUB_TOKEN

## Note
The actual build fails due to a separate code issue in `internal/application/container.go:154`
(assignment mismatch with `appProvider.NewInitializer`). This is unrelated to the Makefile
changes and should be addressed by another feature.
